@startuml UC-BACKLOG-ITEM-REMOVE
' UC-15.4 - Remove Product Backlog Item | semantic key: UC-BACKLOG-ITEM-REMOVE
' Source: data/use_cases/product-backlog/UC-BACKLOG-ITEM-REMOVE.yml
' Business Rules: BR-PRODUCT-OWNER-BACKLOG, BR-PROJECT-ARCHIVED-READ-ONLY
' Trace comments ' [ref] name the YAML element behind the next action.
' No title: the Word caption supplies it.
' One Activity Final shared by all paths (team decision 2026-10-05; UML allows one or several). It
' is reached after the item is removed and recorded (postconditions met) or with the item unchanged
' (AF-01 cancellation, EX-01 rejection).
' Layout (2026-10-06): the decision "Confirm removal?" is drawn in the System lane, where the System
' waits for the Product Owner's answer; the guards name the Product Owner's choice. In the Product
' Owner lane its merge forced a detour across the lanes.
!include ../../_shared/activity-style.puml
|PRO| $lane_title("Product Owner")
|SYS| $lane_title("System")

|PRO|
start
' [NF1]
:Select Product Backlog Item
and request removal;
|SYS|
if ($question_x("Item locked in active Sprint?")) then ($guard_left("[not locked]"))
  ' [NF2]
  :Display impact and
  request confirmation;
  if ($question("Confirm removal?")) then ($guard_left("[confirm]"))
    |PRO|
    ' [NF3]
    :Confirm removal;
    |SYS|
    ' [NF4, POST1, POST2, BR-PRODUCT-OWNER-BACKLOG]
    :Remove item and
    record removal;
  else ($guard_right("[cancel", "— AF-01]"))
    |SYS|
    ' [AF-01.1]
    :Leave Product Backlog
    Item unchanged;
  endif
else ($guard_right("[locked in active", "Sprint — EX-01]"))
  ' [EX-01, GUIDE-7.3]
  :Reject item removal;
endif
|SYS|
stop
@enduml
